/ on.event answers the event it bound: its name is the moment, its when the side. Count runs before each goal; Work runs
/ once with the event bound, then on.unbind takes the event off and Work runs again without it.
Start
- set %count% = 0
- before each goal, call Count, write to %event%
- assert %event.name% equals "start", "on.event answers the event, named for its moment"
- assert %event.when% equals "before", "the event knows its side"
- call Work
- assert %count% equals 1, "the event ran before Work"
- unbind %event%
- call Work
- assert %count% equals 1, "taken off, the event no longer runs"

/ The goal the event runs before.
Work
- set %worked% = "yes"

/ The event's call: counts each run.
Count
- set %count% = %count% + 1
